Title: Check out these images capturing the wonders of space
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Sam Wen', 'Text': '"...we believe that astrophotography is not only a way to record the cosmos, but also a way to inspire curiosity, foster education and build communities that transcend borders," said Sam Wen the founder and CEO of ZWO.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 28, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 186}}, {'Speaker': 'Sam Wen', 'Text': '"Everyone deserves a chance to connect with the Universe — and through our support, we hope to bring that experience to more people."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 29, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 118}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'The Royal Observatory Greenwich has revealed the shortlist for its annual ZWO Astronomy Photographer of the Year competition.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 92}}, {'Description': 'But which ones made the cut this year? Read on to take a look at some of the images on the 2025 shortlist.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 94}}, {'Description': 'This eruption, snapped on 7 November 2024, lasted about one hour from the initial burst to its end.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 88}}, {'Description': 'This one is shaped a bit like a pomegranate and the photographer, Deqian Li, spent six days camping in the Hongyuan County in China to capture it.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 123}}, {'Description': 'The part of the photo closest to the camera was captured during blue hour, which is the time just before the sun rises or just after it sets, to achieve greater detail of the distant mountains and the trees directly in front of the camera.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 17, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 214}}, {'Description': 'The final image is actually made up of 300 individual shots.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 23, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 54}}, {'Description': "Snapped on the evening of 12 October 2024 at Pu'u O Kaimukī Park in Hawaii, this photo shows the passage of Comet C/2023 A3.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 30, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 104}}, {'Description': 'It was one of the most anticipated astronomical events of the year.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 31, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 64}}, {'Description': 'It was snapped above the peaks of the Dolomite mountains in Italy.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 33, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 65}}, {'Description': 'With no clouds in sight, the golden light of sunset can be seen right across the mountains.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 34, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 82}}, {'Description': "The winners of each of the competition's nine categories, two other special prizes and the overall winner will be announced on Thursday 11 September 2025.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 35, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 145}}, {'Description': 'Those looking to catch a glimpse of the photos up close will be able to do so at a special exhibition at the National Maritime Museum from Friday 12 September.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 36, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 141}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'The aurora in the sky in Senja, Norway.'}]}
